The question asks whether property hooks (get/set directly in property declaration) were introduced in PHP 8.4.

Let me recall: Property hooks were indeed introduced in PHP 8.4. This allows you to define `get` and `set` hooks directly in a property declaration, like:

```php
class Person {
    public string $name {
        get {
            return ucfirst($this->name);
        }
        set {
            $this->name = strtolower($value);
        }
    }
}
```

Yes, this is correct — property hooks were introduced in PHP 8.4.
